{
  "description": "The automatic order of usage accounts that Overview and the All accounts widget share, against the stored order other consumers keep. Rule: (1) accounts whose connection is reconnectRequired (expired sign-in) come first; every other connection, including unknown with a failed reading, is one group. (2) Within each group, rank by the account headline at now (the account-headline.json rule, reset-due windows included) by its unrounded remaining percentage, lowest first. A headline that is exhausted (provider flag, or exactly 0 left) ranks as 0 whatever its figure. A headline whose percentage is unknown (missing, non-finite or outside 0-100) and not exhausted, a reading with no windows, and no reading at all rank after every known figure in the group. (3) Ties go to the earlier createdAt, then to the id compared by Unicode scalar values (not UTF-16 code units, not locale collation, not canonical equivalence). Display mode never enters the order. The stored order is the order the accounts are listed in and no reading changes it: pins, Provider scope and the export keep it. Custom keeps its saved ids in saved order, an id counted once and an id whose account is gone dropped. Times are epoch milliseconds. Expected lists are written by hand from the rule, never generated from an implementation.",
  "schema": "vectors: array of { name: string (unique, says what the case proves); now: number; accounts: array, in stored order, of { id: string; createdAt: number; connection: \"connected\" | \"reconnectRequired\" | \"unknown\"; reading: null (no reading yet; connection is then \"unknown\") or { fetchedAt: number; status: \"ok\" | \"partial\" | \"failed\"; windows: array of { id: string; scope: \"global\" | \"model\" | \"unknown\"; remainingPercent: number or null; exhausted: boolean; resetAt: number or null } in provider order } }; custom: array of string (a Custom selection's saved ids, in saved order); expected: { automatic: array of string (Overview and All accounts); stored: array of string; custom: array of string } }. Every key is present in every object, null where the value is absent.",
